 ## Background
-The method was introduced by A.P. Yushchenko in the paper "Marching cubes 33: construction of topologically correct isosurfaces" [S1]. It was implemented in the HIGZ graphics package as part of the PAW (Physics Analysis Workstation) project at CERN (European Organization for Nuclear Research) [S1]. The work addresses the limitations of the original Marching Cubes algorithm by Lorensen and Cline (1987) [S1], specifically the topological discrepancies arising from the 15-case lookup table.
+The method was introduced to address the limitations of the original Marching Cubes algorithm by Lorensen and Cline (1987) [S1]. It was implemented in the HIGZ graphics package [S1]. The work addresses the topological discrepancies arising from the 15-case lookup table by expanding the configuration set to 33 topologically distinct patterns permitted by the trilinear function [S1].
 
